ok   take axis=None works on the flattened array
ok   take on an empty index list returns an empty array of shape (0,)
ok   put mode='wrap' with v shorter than ind ('it will be repeated as necessary')
ok   put mode='clip' with v shorter than ind ('it will be repeated as necessary')
ok   put mode='raise': negative index counts from the end; out-of-range raises IndexError
ok   put acts on the flattened target ('a.flat[ind] = v')
ok   putmask docstring example ([[0,1,2],[9,16,25]])
