ok   np.diag of 2-D also returns the read-only diagonal view
ok   diagonal offsets and axis1/axis2 on 3-D: result's last axis is the diagonal
ok   diagonal axis1 == axis2 raises ValueError
ok   fill_diagonal tall wrap=False: only the first N rows ([5,0,0],[0,5,0],[0,0,5], rest 0)
ok   fill_diagonal wrap=True: flat step ncols+1 continues after the square block (docstring 7x3: rows 0,1,2,4,5,6)  [[4, 0, 0], [0, 4, 0], [0, 0, 4], [0, 0, 0], [4, 0, 0], [0, 4, 0], [0, 0, 4]]
ok   fill_diagonal wide array and val sequence (repeated/truncated to the diagonal)
ok   fill_diagonal with shorter val repeats it cyclically
ok   fill_diagonal 3-D: a[i,i,i] only
ok   fill_diagonal on a non-hypercube N-D (N>2) raises ValueError ('All dimensions of input must be of equal length')
