ok   where 1-arg = nonzero
ok   where broadcasting (3,1) cond with (4,) x
---- apply_along_axis / vectorize / frompyfunc
ok   apply_along_axis scalar result: axis removed (docstring my_func -> [4., 5., 6.])
ok   apply_along_axis 1-D result replaces the axis (sorted rows)
ok   apply_along_axis 2-D result: the axis is replaced by the result's dims (docstring (3,3,3))
   apply_along_axis where the first call returns int 0 and later calls floats -> [0, 2, 4] dtype int64 (output buffer is allocated from the first result's dtype; not documented)
ok   apply_along_axis pitfall recorded: output dtype follows the FIRST call (later floats truncated)
ok   apply_along_axis on an axis of length 0 raises ValueError ('Cannot apply_along_axis when any iteration dimensions are 0')
ok   apply_along_axis 3-D axis=1 = per-fibre cumsum
ok   vectorize without otypes calls the function on the first element one extra time (documented: cache=True prevents 'calling the function twice')  [1, 1, 2, 3]
ok   vectorize cache=True calls the function exactly once per element
ok   vectorize with otypes calls once per element
ok   vectorize first-call inference pitfall: 'output type determined by calling the function with the first element' -> int, fractions lost  [0, 1, 2]
